{
  "_doc": [
    "Intents of barch-voice (voice.py). The sentence is normalized before matching: lower case,",
    "no accents, no punctuation, fillers like 'por favor' removed, the wake word gone. Write the",
    "patterns that way (regex, matched whole, case-insensitive is not needed). Named groups feed",
    "the templates: {app}, {proj}, {palette}, {scene}, {region}, {n_x} (a number, in words or",
    "digits), {verb} with 'onoff' → {onoff} on|off and {onoff_pt}. kinds: exec (run, argv),",
    "spawn (detached), hypr (dispatch, Lua expression), app, project (with: claude|nvim|files|''),",
    "palette, scene, region, confirm (ask, then run on 'sim'), say, time, date, health, remind,",
    "claude (force the fallback), pause, hush. 'say' is spoken; without it a short chime plays.",
    "Test without a microphone: barch voice test \"abre o terminal\"."
  ],
  "app_aliases": {
    "terminal": "foot",
    "console": "foot",
    "shell": "foot",
    "navegador": "browser",
    "browser": "browser",
    "internet": "browser",
    "mullvad": "mullvad-browser.desktop",
    "brave": "brave-origin.desktop",
    "chromium": "chromium.desktop",
